# Your own settings for building and releasing the game.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local at the top of the folder and change what you need. Git ignores
# .env.local, so your settings stay on your machine. Everything here has a default, so the game
# builds without it; you need it once you release a game of your own.
#
# Secrets (signing passwords, store credentials) don't go here: they go in .env, which docs/RELEASE.md
# describes.

# Your app's ID. Both stores fix it on the first upload, so choose it once: reverse-domain style,
# lower case, e.g. com.yourname.mygame. The default is One More Story's, which you can't publish under.
# APP_ID=com.yourname.mygame

# The name under the icon on the phone.
# APP_TITLE=My Game

# Where the Android SDK is. The default is where .NET's installer puts it on a Mac.
#   Windows: C:/Users/<you>/AppData/Local/Android/Sdk
# ANDROID_SDK=/Users/<you>/Library/Android/sdk

# A JDK 21 to build Android with. The default asks macOS for one.
#   Windows: C:/Program Files/Microsoft/jdk-21.0.5.11-hotspot
# JDK=/Library/Java/JavaVirtualMachines/microsoft-21.jdk/Contents/Home

# Your App Store Connect API key file (the .p8 Apple lets you download once). Only `make asc-status`
# needs it. Keep the file outside this folder.
# APPLE_P8=/Users/<you>/keys/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8
